From 23d55aeafa8ec063ff6fcf977cba8d52c2fe3c1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:36:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: bake in LFB + 16bpp hints, matching doskutsu's own
 defaults

Real-hardware investigation (2026-08-30/31, 486DX2-66 + S3 ViRGE, see
docs/PLAN.md's "Phase 0/2 result") found this port ran banked/32bpp by
default, unlike doskutsu, which unconditionally forces LFB
(nxengine-evo patch 0045) and caps color depth at 16bpp (patch 0041)
on every DOS build. Matching that config here fixed an intermittent
launch-time video-corruption bug (a zero-settle-delay bank-switch race
in the shared backend that LFB sidesteps entirely) and measured a real
fps improvement (13.25fps vs. 12.4-12.7fps at 32bpp, same rig) from
halving per-pixel data volume.

Tonight's testing used manual SET SDL_DOS_PREFER_LFB=1 / SET
SDL_DOS_MAX_BPP=16 before every run; this bakes the same config into
the port itself via SDL_SetHintWithPriority (SDL_HINT_OVERRIDE),
unconditionally, matching doskutsu's own call site and priority.

Not yet real-hardware-confirmed safe on Mach64 or Cirrus. Expected to
be a no-op on both (Mach64 has no LFB silicon at all; Cirrus already
auto-disables LFB at the shared layer regardless of what a port
requests, SDL/0019+0020) -- but the MAX_BPP=16 cap genuinely changes
what VESA mode Mach64 negotiates (previously 640x480 24bpp banked,
closest-match fallback since no 320x240 exists on that chip) to an
untested 640x480-16bpp-or-lower alternative. Needs real-hardware
verification on both cards before this is fully trusted there.
---
 gameSource/game.cpp | 30 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gameSource/game.cpp b/gameSource/game.cpp
index 2051c4d..18737f0 100644
--- a/gameSource/game.cpp
+++ b/gameSource/game.cpp
@@ -642,6 +642,36 @@ int mainFunction( int inArgCount, char **inArgs ) {
     // confirmation of the boot log's negotiated mode does. Set
     // regardless since it's a no-op when not needed.
     SDL_SetHint( SDL_HINT_DOS_PIN_WINDOW_TO_NATIVE_MODE, "1" );
+
+    // DOS-PORT: force LFB and cap color depth at 16bpp, matching sibling
+    // port doskutsu's own unconditional hints (nxengine-evo patches
+    // 0045/0041) on every card, every DOS build. Found via real-hardware
+    // investigation (2026-08-30/31, see docs/PLAN.md's "Phase 0/2
+    // result") on a 486DX2-66 + S3 ViRGE rig: this port previously ran
+    // banked/32bpp by default (unlike doskutsu), which produced an
+    // intermittent launch-time video-corruption bug (zero-settle-delay
+    // bank-switch race in the shared backend, `SDL_dosframebuffer.c`) --
+    // forcing LFB avoids that bank-switched write path entirely. The
+    // 16bpp cap is a real, measured fps win on top (13.25fps vs.
+    // 12.4-12.7fps at 32bpp, same rig) by halving per-pixel data volume.
+    // A separate, still-unexplained runtime video-corruption symptom on
+    // that same rig turned out to be an audio/DMA interaction, not a
+    // video-mode issue -- these hints alone did not fix it; see
+    // docs/PLAN.md for the full chain. Set unconditionally like
+    // doskutsu's own hints: on Mach64 (no LFB silicon at all) and Cirrus
+    // (LFB auto-disabled by a separate shared-layer fix, SDL/0019/0020,
+    // regardless of what this hint requests) `SDL_HINT_DOS_PREFER_LFB`
+    // is expected to be a safe no-op -- NOT yet real-hardware-confirmed
+    // on either card as of this patch; the `SDL_HINT_DOS_MAX_BPP=16` cap
+    // in particular changes what VESA mode Mach64 negotiates (previously
+    // 640x480 24bpp banked, closest-match since no 320x240 exists on
+    // that chip) to an untested 640x480 16bpp-or-lower alternative --
+    // needs real-hardware verification on Mach64/Cirrus before this
+    // hint pair can be trusted there the way it now is on ViRGE.
+    SDL_SetHintWithPriority( SDL_HINT_DOS_PREFER_LFB, "1",
+                              SDL_HINT_OVERRIDE );
+    SDL_SetHintWithPriority( SDL_HINT_DOS_MAX_BPP, "16",
+                              SDL_HINT_OVERRIDE );
 #endif
 
     // DOS-PORT: SDL3 removed SDL_INIT_NOPARACHUTE (no signal-handler
